  "english": "11. Monday, Tone 2 [AK]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Father [Harts] (Kamavorial anoun ko yavidian) \"Glorified is your name forever.\"\n\n17. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Exaltation of the Cross. Until the tenth Sunday, see the First Volume; but for the Father [harts] of the martyrs and of the fasts, and the Resurrection Ascension [Hambartsis] hymns, and the tone of the days, see the 4th Directory, keeping only these dates.\n\nNovember:\n\n19. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Tenth [Sunday]. Eve of the Fast of the Advent [Yisnakats]. Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 7 [DZ]: (Or ee verd) \"You who are above,\" see to the end.\n\n20. Monday, Tone 8 [DK]. Fast of Advent [Yisnakats]. Father [Harts] of the Fast: (Tshmardabes) \"Truly.\"\n\n21. Tuesday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n\n25. Saturday, Tone 6 [GZ]. [Feast of] Gregory and Nicholas the Wonderworker bishops, and the other bishop Nicholas, and Myron the bishop. Children [Mankunk], proper: (Hiatzan) \"They were amazed.\" Midday [Tshashu] Hymn, Tone 2: (Or loosov) \"Who with light.\"\n\n26. Sunday, Tone 5 [GK]. First [Sunday]. Father [Harts], Tone 2 [AK]: (Anasgizpn band) \"Unoriginate Word.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [GK]: (Uzko yaroutiunt) \"Your Resurrection,\" and (Arial) \"Having taken.\"\n\n27. Monday, Tone 7 [DZ]. [Feast of] Julian and Vasilouhi. Father [Harts], Tone 7 [DZ]: (Housatzialkn) \"Those who hoped.\"\nAnd for the others, see until the end in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember:\n\n3. Sunday, Tone 6 [GZ]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Harts], Tone 3 [BZ]: (Or takavort es) \"You who are King.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [GZ]: (Paravorial e ko yaroutiunt) \"Glorified is your Resurrection.\"\n\n4. Monday, Tone 5 [GK]. [Feast of] Genarios the bishop, and Mercurius the soldier, and of Yakovik and Iravapar.\n\n5. Tuesday, Tone 7 [DZ]. [Feast of] Abgar the king.\n\n6. Wednesday, Tone 8 [DK]. Father [Harts] of the Fast, Tone 8 [DK]: (Orhnial der astvad) \"Blessed are you, Lord God.\"\n\n9. Saturday, Tone 3 [BDZ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n10. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Third [Sunday]. Eve of the Fast of Saint James [Surb Hakob]. Father [Harts], Tone 4 [BK]: (Or uzdzarayi) \"Who [the image] of the servant.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [BK]: (Gankhetsin) \"They anticipated.\"\n\n17. Sunday, Tone 6 [GZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Harts], Tone 6 [GZ]: (Or yavidanitz) \"Who from eternity.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [BZ]: (Aysor zvartshatzial) \"Today rejoicing.\"\n\n23. Saturday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. [Feast of] David the prophet and James the apostle.\n\n24. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father [Harts], Tone 5 [GK]: (Nakhayavidian) \"Before eternity.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [AK]: (Skancheli) \"Wonderful\" and (Hrashali zyaroutiun) \"Wondrous Resurrection.\"\n\n29. Friday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Eve of the Nativity Fast.\n\n30. Saturday, Tone 8 [DK]. Fast of the Nativity. —[Feast of] Basil of Caesarea, etc.\n\n31. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Sixth [Sunday] of the Fast. Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [ADZ]: (Sosgali desil hreshdagin) \"The awesome sight of the angel,\" to the end.\n\nJanuary:\n\n1. Monday, Tone 2 [AK]. Fast. Father [Harts] of the Fast, Tone 8 [DK]: (Astvad hartzn merotz pare) \"God of our fathers, beneficent.\"\n\n2. Tuesday, Tone 6 [GZ]. Fast. Father [Harts] of the Fast, Tone 1 [ADZ]: (Yerkein mangunkn) \"The children sang.\"\n\n5. Friday, Tone 5 [GK]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ our God.\n[corrupt/untranslated run of characters]\n[corrupt/untranslated run of characters]\nSeven-day cycle of the Romans 6.\n\nJanuary:\n[corrupt/untranslated characters]\n\n6. THURSDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ our God. The period of eating [non-fast days] is eleven days.\n[corrupt/untranslated characters]\n[corrupt/untranslated characters]\n\n13. Thursday. Eighth day of the Nativity of Christ.\n[corrupt/untranslated characters]\n\n15. Saturday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n\n16. Sunday. Eve of the Fast of the Catechumens [Arachtzavor]. Father [Harts], Tone 7 [DZ]: (Dakoomn miadzni) \"The dawning of the Only-begotten.\"",
